# Build output. 1.7 GB of cargo artifacts; the corpus runner also defaults
# MINE to target/debug/textrill, so this path is load-bearing, not just noise.
textrill/target/

# The native GUI crate's build output. It has its own lockfile, which is
# tracked, so only `target/` is ignored here.
textrill-gui-rs/target/

# The reference (Perl) checkout the differential harness compares against.
# Derived: `make ref` extracts the tracked txt2html-3.0.tar.gz (from
# research/) into ref/ and copies the tracked stub at stubs/YAML/Syck.pm into
# ref/stubs/. Both halves are reproducible offline, so nothing under ref/ is
# versioned. The canonical stub lives at stubs/ precisely so its reasoning is
# reviewable -- a stub that exists only on one machine is how the gate became
# unreproducible in the first place.
ref/

# The retired Python virtualenv (maturin/PySide6). Nothing in the build uses it
# now, but it is still on disk, so it stays ignored rather than dirtying the
# tree.
.venv/

# Packaging droppings from the retired Python packages. The Python GUI is
# archived under legacy-archive/; a stray build there should not dirty the tree
# if someone ever runs it again.
*.egg-info/
legacy-archive/textrill-gui/build/
legacy-archive/textrill-gui/dist/

# Python bytecode from the corpus runner and the fuzzer.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor and OS droppings.
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store

# Competitive research material. The tarballs are tracked, exactly as
# txt2html-3.0.tar.gz is, so the studies in docs/ can be re-run offline by
# anyone. A tree extracted from them is derived and ignored.
research/pandoc/*/

# Generated by `make cargo-sources`; see the Flatpak packaging note.
packaging/cargo-sources.json
